e enough time to go into  every little detail but in the books I  still fully believe we will find out the  Starks and the White Walkers are related  in some way there are just way too many  connections between the Starks and the  White Walkers for them not to be  after all the Starks words our winter is  coming their houses Winterfell  their house sword is called ice their  crypts a wonderful are full of dead  kings of winter which basically  describes exactly what the night king is  or was all of this in my opinion  directly relates to the White Walkers  that's why the Starks Castle was created  directly after the first long night  ended as soon as the White Walkers were  defeated the first time they needed to  make sure they can never make it south  again so that's when Brandon the Builder  made the wall then he made Winterfell  the wall was the first line of defense  against the White Walkers but if they  ever made it through that wall  Winterfell would be the next line of  defense this is why a stark must always  remain in Winterfell  so that if the day should ever come when  the White Walkers invaded again it would  need to be a stark that defeats them in  some way now I know there are many fans  that are upset about the night King  getting defeated so early but I expected  him to lose at Winterfell  the Starks house was always meant to be  the location of the White Walkers deep  this is where winter will fall I have  made several videos on all those  connections before I will make sure to  leave a link in the description if any  of you want to check them out so like I  said earlier I would have definitely  like to see John fight the night king in  a 1 versus 1 sword fight as you all know  this has been John's mission ever since  he found out about the army of the Dead  which was in the very first season of  the show he basically spent his entire  life focusing on defeating them however  if John was not going to be the one to  kill the night king I am still ki